# Upstream Arch package -> Debian source. See AGENTS.md, rule 4.
# <arch-name> <debian-name>             same name or Debian rename
# <arch-name> source:<kind> [note]      no Debian package:
#   armbian-platform  Armbian kernel, firmware and board support
#   arch-only         Arch tooling, replaced by an entry in adapt.list
#   armbian-build     build in armbian/external: todo. Built ones map to their package name.
#   vendor            vendor repository, release or Flathub: todo
# Extra lines (lua, cryptsetup, util-linux, alsa-lib, a second libpulse) map Arch base
# packages that provide commands Omarchy calls. Upstream lists do not name them.
# superwhisper-bin lines after the first: the vendor installer's apt
# dependencies, so it runs without sudo (transform 90-superwhisper-vendor-installer).
